{{also|tinte|tinté|tintē}}
==Dutch==

===Etymology===
Attested as ''Tente'' in the 16th century. Likely derived from {{inh|nl|dum|tinte|t=tent, temporary shelter}}. Proposed derivations from {{cog|ML.|tincta|t=tincture, paint}} (as a reference to madder production) or {{cog|dum|tinte|t=notched lower section of an arrow}} (as a reference to shape of the polder the village is located in) are significantly less likely.

See also {{cog|zea|De Tinte}}. 

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/ˈtɪn.tə/}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|Tin|te}}
* {{rhymes|nl|ɪntə|s=2}}

